{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>All the days of my service</b> — my appointed time." "<b>My changing</b> — my death, from והאלילים כליל יחלוף, or my going, like 'חלף הלך לו' (he passed on, he went), for the one born is called 'coming,' and the dead is called 'going,' like 'a generation goes and a generation comes.' 'I am going the way of all the earth.'"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The phrase זמני ('my appointed time') is given as the gloss for the lemma; the strange מן והאלילים in comment 1 may indicate textual corruption in this region of the manuscript.", 1 "The phrase מן והאלילים כליל יחלוף is textually obscure, possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally as transmitted. The verse citations are 1 Kings 10:13 (or Jer. 9:15), Ecclesiastes 1:4, and 1 Kings 2:2 respectively."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:37.843703081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}